@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Secure Code Analysis & Compliance Policies";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Secure code analysis and compliance policies are essential in DevOps to identify vulnerabilities, enforce security standards, and ensure regulatory compliance. By integrating these practices into CI/CD pipelines, organizations can maintain secure and high-quality software releases.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Why is Secure Code Analysis Important?</h2>
        <p>Secure code analysis helps detect security vulnerabilities in the development phase, reducing risks and improving software quality. Key benefits include:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Early Detection:</strong> Identifies security flaws before production deployment.</li>
            <li><strong>Compliance Enforcement:</strong> Ensures adherence to security and regulatory standards.</li>
            <li><strong>Automated Security Checks:</strong> Integrates with CI/CD pipelines for continuous scanning.</li>
            <li><strong>Reduction in Attack Surface:</strong> Prevents exploits by fixing insecure code.</li>
            <li><strong>Faster Incident Response:</strong> Provides insights for quick remediation of vulnerabilities.</li>
            <li><strong>Improved Code Quality:</strong> Enforces best practices in secure software development.</li>
            <li><strong>Lower Remediation Costs:</strong> Fixing vulnerabilities during development is cheaper than post-deployment.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-4">
        <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/security/media/secure-code-analysis.png" alt="Secure Code Analysis" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
        <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Secure Code Analysis in Azure DevOps</small></p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Types of Secure Code Analysis</h2>
        <p>There are multiple approaches to securing software through automated analysis:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Static Application Security Testing (SAST):</strong> Analyzes source code for vulnerabilities before execution.</li>
            <li><strong>Dynamic Application Security Testing (DAST):</strong> Simulates attacks on a running application to detect security flaws.</li>
            <li><strong>Interactive Application Security Testing (IAST):</strong> Combines static and dynamic testing for more comprehensive security analysis.</li>
            <li><strong>Software Composition Analysis (SCA):</strong> Scans open-source dependencies for known vulnerabilities.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Implementing Secure Code Analysis in Azure DevOps</h2>
        <p>Follow these steps to integrate secure code analysis:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Enable Static Code Analysis:</strong> Use tools like SonarQube, WhiteSource, or GitHub Advanced Security.</li>
            <li><strong>Scan for Open Source Vulnerabilities:</strong> Automate dependency scanning with tools like Dependabot or Snyk.</li>
            <li><strong>Integrate Security into CI/CD:</strong> Add security scanning as part of the build and release pipelines.</li>
            <li><strong>Apply Secure Coding Standards:</strong> Use industry best practices such as OWASP Top 10 and CIS benchmarks.</li>
            <li><strong>Review Security Reports:</strong> Analyze reports for vulnerabilities and prioritize fixes.</li>
            <li><strong>Implement Automated Remediation:</strong> Use AI-powered tools to suggest and apply security patches.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Example YAML for Secure Code Scanning</h3>
        <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">
steps:
- task: SonarQubeAnalyze@4
  inputs:
    scannerMode: 'CLI'
    configMode: 'manual'
    sonarProjectKey: 'MyProject'
    sonarProjectName: 'SecureApp'
- task: WhiteSource@21
  inputs:
    organizationServiceConnection: 'MyAzureConnection'
    scanType: 'Full'
    failBuildOnPolicyViolation: true
        </pre>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Compliance Policies in Azure DevOps</h3>
        <p>Compliance policies help enforce security guidelines and regulatory requirements to maintain the integrity of software deployments.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Define Policy Requirements:</strong> Set rules for code quality, security, and access controls.</li>
            <li><strong>Implement Branch Policies:</strong> Require code reviews, automated tests, and security scans before merging.</li>
            <li><strong>Enforce Access Control:</strong> Use RBAC and conditional access policies to manage user permissions.</li>
            <li><strong>Monitor & Audit:</strong> Track policy violations using Azure Security Center and Compliance Manager.</li>
            <li><strong>Automate Compliance Checks:</strong> Use security gates in CI/CD pipelines to prevent insecure deployments.</li>
            <li><strong>Implement Data Protection Measures:</strong> Encrypt sensitive data and apply secure storage policies.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Best Practices for Secure Code Analysis & Compliance</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Shift Left Security:</strong> Perform security analysis early in the development lifecycle.</li>
            <li><strong>Use Multiple Scanning Tools:</strong> Combine SAST, DAST, and SCA for comprehensive security coverage.</li>
            <li><strong>Train Developers in Secure Coding:</strong> Conduct security awareness training for development teams.</li>
            <li><strong>Automate Security Policies:</strong> Implement policy-as-code to enforce security standards.</li>
            <li><strong>Regularly Update Security Rules:</strong> Keep scanning tools up to date with the latest vulnerability definitions.</li>
            <li><strong>Monitor & Respond to Security Threats:</strong> Use real-time alerts for high-risk vulnerabilities.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <p>By integrating secure code analysis and compliance policies into DevOps workflows, organizations can improve security, reduce risks, and maintain compliance with industry standards. Automating security within CI/CD pipelines helps detect and fix vulnerabilities before they become a threat.</p>
    </div>

